---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lessons = [
  {
    number: 57,
    title: "Making It Feel Right",
    description: "Tune controls with fixed steps, easing, and trace HUDs.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 58,
    title: "Squeezing Speed",
    description: "Profile hotspots, cache data, and unroll loops for speed.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 59,
    title: "When BASIC Breaks",
    description: "Handle DATA, memory, and input failures gracefully.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 60,
    title: "Under the Skin",
    description: "Inspect BASIC pointers, screen RAM, and colour memory.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 61,
    title: "POKE the Future",
    description: "Install machine code helpers and call them with SYS.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 62,
    title: "Looking Below",
    description: "Compare BASIC routines with their assembly equivalents.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 63,
    title: "The Threshold",
    description: "Monitor frame budgets and decide what to port next.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 64,
    title: "Retrospective: The Journey So Far",
    description: "Celebrate the course and prepare for the Transition module.",
    status: "available"
  }
];
---

<Layout title="Week 8: Hitting the Limits - Commodore 64">
  <style>
    .course-hero {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0ea5e9 0%, #0369a1 100%);
      color: white;
      padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-4);
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .course-title {
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
      font-weight: 900;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
      text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
    }

    .course-subtitle {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      opacity: 0.95;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    }

    .course-description {
      max-width: 720px;
      margin: 0 auto var(--space-8);
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      opacity: 0.95;
    }

    .content-container {
      max-width: 1000px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 var(--space-4);
    }

    .section-title {
      font-size: 2rem;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .intro-section {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid #0ea5e9;
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-8);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .intro-section h2 {
      color: #0ea5e9;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .lessons-grid {
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-4);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .lesson-card {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid var(--color-border);
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-6);
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto;
      gap: var(--space-4);
      align-items: center;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: var(--color-text);
      transition: all var(--transition-base);
    }

    .lesson-card:hover {
      border-color: #0ea5e9;
      transform: translateX(4px);
      box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.12);
    }

    .lesson-number {
      width: 50px;
      height: 50px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0ea5e9 0%, #0369a1 100%);
      color: white;
      border-radius: 50%;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    .lesson-title {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
    }

    .lesson-description {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .lesson-status {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--space-2);
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      font-weight: 500;
      padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
      border-radius: 9999px;
      background: rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.12);
      color: #0ea5e9;
    }

    .start-button {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-8);
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0ea5e9 0%, #0369a1 100%);
      color: white;
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      text-decoration: none;
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      transition: all var(--transition-base);
    }

    .start-button:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
      box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.3);
    }
  </style>

  <section class="course-hero">
    <h1 class="course-title">WEEK 8: HITTING THE LIMITS</h1>
    <p class="course-subtitle">Feel, performance, machine-code helpers, final retrospective</p>
    <p class="course-description">
      Week 8 answers the big question: “What happens when BASIC isn’t enough?” You’ll tune responsiveness, squeeze the
      interpreter for speed, guard against crashes, peek inside memory, call machine code, compare BASIC with assembly,
      and decide what to move below the language. We finish with a reflective retrospective that prepares you for the
      Transition course.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="content-container">
    <section class="intro-section">
      <h2>What You’ll Explore</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Lesson 57:</strong> Tune controls with fixed-step loops and easing.</li>
        <li><strong>Lesson 58:</strong> Profile loops, cache data, and unroll work for raw speed.</li>
        <li><strong>Lesson 59:</strong> Catch BASIC’s error conditions gracefully.</li>
        <li><strong>Lesson 60:</strong> Inspect pointers, screen RAM, and colour memory.</li>
        <li><strong>Lesson 61:</strong> Install and call a machine-code helper from BASIC.</li>
        <li><strong>Lesson 62:</strong> Compare BASIC logic with its assembly counterpart.</li>
        <li><strong>Lesson 63:</strong> Decide what to port by tracking frame budgets.</li>
        <li><strong>Lesson 64:</strong> Reflect, plan, and transition to the next course.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">Lessons</h2>
      <div class="lessons-grid">
        {lessons.map(lesson => (
          <a href={`/commodore-64/basic/week-8/lesson-${String(lesson.number).padStart(2, '0')}`}
             class="lesson-card">
            <div class="lesson-number">{lesson.number}</div>
            <div class="lesson-content">
              <h3 class="lesson-title">{lesson.title}</h3>
              <p class="lesson-description">{lesson.description}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lesson-status">Start →</div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section style="text-align: center; margin: var(--space-16) 0;">
      <h2 class="section-title">Ready to Cross the Threshold?</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); max-width: 600px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
        Week 8 shows you where BASIC bends and where it breaks. Capture the lessons, celebrate the journey, and get
        ready to talk directly to the metal in the Transition course.
      </p>
      <a href="/commodore-64/basic/week-8/lesson-57" class="start-button">Start Lesson 57: Making It Feel Right</a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
